<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pribislav-Henry</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1150</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Pribislav of Brandenburg, Henry Pribislav</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pribislav-Henry was the last prince of the Slavic Hevelli, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>. A Christian who took the baptismal name Henry, he allied himself with the German margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-the-bear">Albert the Bear</a> and made him his heir. On his death in 1150 Albert took over Brandenburg, and after securing it in 1157 founded the March of Brandenburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pribislav-henry.jpg" alt="Pribislav-Henry" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Max Unger (sculptor) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OttoI_Gruppe_Siegesallee.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
